1. General
a. Discard old builds : Automatically deletes old build history to save disk space.
b. Do not allow concurrent builds : Allows only one build at a time. A new build waits until the previous one finishes
c. Do not allow the pipeline to resume if the controller restarts : If Jenkins restarts while the pipeline is running, the pipeline will not continue from where it stopped.
d. GitHub project : Links the Jenkins job to the GitHub repository/project.
e. Pipeline speed/durability override : Controls the balance between pipeline performance and reliability when Jenkins is restarted.1
f. This project is parameterised : Allows you to provide input values when starting the build, such as ENV_NAME=QA, BROWSER=chrome, etc.
g. Throttle builds : Limits how many builds of this job can run at the same time, based on configured throttling rules. Time period like second, minutes and hours etc.


